<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">linebreaker</ansi>

The Linebreaker is the neutral elite of the Vanguard. It turns its column into
a wall: allies behind it take less damage from every blow, and its Brace
answers more than one foe.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Shield line     allies in its column take 10% less damage while it
                     stands (columns take the best cut; they don't stack)
  35 Plated greaves  +4 armor
  40 Parrying wall   +4 parry chance
  45 Deeper line     its column takes 15% less damage
  50 Unbroken        +8% maximum health
  55 Iron wall       +4 armor and +3 Attack
  60 Twin brace      Brace answers the first two foes that strike into its
                     column

It needs the Vanguard first (<ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] linebreaker confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Halberdier talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Iron Hide (+5 Armor), Veteran's
Edge (+3 Attack), Second Wind (once a battle, below a quarter of its health at
the start of its turn, heals a tenth of its maximum). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
